 ; אֲהוּבָה Deut 21:15 (twice in verse); 21:16 . &#8212; love (mostly with accusative, followed by לְ + object Lev 19:18 , 34 ; 2Chr 19:2 (late), followed by בְּ Eccl 5:9 ; absolute 3:8 & see below), (affection both pure & impure, divine & human); — 1 human love to human object ; absolute, opposed to hate שָׂנֵא Eccl 3:8 ; of love to son Gen 22:2 ; 25:28 ; 37:3-4 , 44:20 (JE) Prov 13:24 ; so also 2Sam 13:21 ᵐ5 Ew Th We, compare Dr, of David's loving Amnon; never to parent, but mother-in-law Ruth 4:15 ; of man's love to woman; wife Gen 24:67 ; 29:20 , 30 (compare 29:18 ):32 (JE), also Deut 21:15 (twice in verse); 21:16 ; Judg 14:16 ; 1Sam 1:5 ; 2Chr 11:21 ; Est 2:17 ; Hosea 3:1 ; Eccl 9:9 ; but also Gen 34:3 (J) Judg 16:4 , 15 ; 2Sam 13:1 , 4 , 15 (where of carnal desire) 1Kin 11:1 compare 11:2 ; Hosea 3:1 ; ׳א רֵעַ loving a paramour , see Ba NB 176 ; woman's love to man 1Sam 18:20 (so 18:28 ᵑ0 , but read ᵐ5 אֹתוֺ אֹהֵב כָליִֿשְׂרָאֵל וְבִי We Dr) Song 1:3-4 , 7 ; 3:1-2 , 3 , 4 (5 t. subject נַפְשִׁי ); compare also figurative of adulterous Judah Jer 2:25 ; Isa 57:8 ; Ezek 16:37 ; of love of slave to master Exod 21:5 (JE) Deut 15:16 ; inferior to superior 1Sam 18:22 compare 18:16 ; love to neighbour Lev 19:18 ( כָּמוֺ֑ךָ לְרֵעֲךָ וְאָהַבְתָּ ), partic to stranger 19:34 (both P), Deut 10:18-19 , love of friend to friend 1Sam 16:21 ; 18:1 , 3 ; 20:17 (twice in verse); Job 19:19 ; Prov 17:1 compare 2Sam 19:7 (twice in verse); 2Chr 19:2 ; see also Prov 9:8 ; 16:13 ; compare 15:12 ; see especially Participle below 2 less often of appetite, object food , Gen 27:7 , 9 , 14 (JE); drink Hosea 3:1 ; Prov 21:17 ; husbandry 2Chr 26:10 ; compare figurative of Ephraim Hosea 10:11 followed by infinitive; length of life Psa 34:13 ; of cupidity Hosea 9:1 ; 1Sam 1:23 ; Eccl 5:9 (twice in verse); of love of sleep Prov 20:13 compare figurative of sluggish watchmen (followed by infinitive) Isa 56:10 ; also with object abstract wisdom (personified), knowledge, righteousness, etc. Prov 4:6 ; 8:17 , 21 ; 12:1 ; 22:11 ; 29:3 ; Amos 5:15 ; Micah 6:8 (infinitive || infinitives) Zech 8:19 , compare Prov 19:8 נַפְשׁוֺ אֹהֵב לֵב קֹנֶה ; object folly, evil, etc., Micah 3:2 ; 4:3 ; Psa 11:5 ; 52:5 ; 52:6 ; 109:17 ; Prov 1:22 ; 8:36 ; 17:19 (twice in verse), compare 18:21 ; Zech 8:17 , compare ׳א כֵּן Amos 4:5 ; Jer 5:3 , followed by Infinitive Hosea 12:8 ; Jer 14:10 , especially of idolatry Hosea 4:13 (where strike out הֵבוּ compare Kö 1. p. 395 ) Jer 8:2 . 3 love to God Exod 20:6 (JE) elsewhere Hexateuch only Deut 5:10 ; 6:5 ; 7:9 9 t. Deuteronomy + Josh 22:5 ; 23:11 ; also Judg 5:31 ; 1Kin 3:3 ; Neh 1:5 ; Dan 9:4 ; especially in (late) Psa 31:24 ; 116:1 ; 145:20 , but usually followed by name, law, etc. of ׳י 5:12 ; 26:8 ; 40:17 ; Psalm 69:37; 70:5 ; 97:10 ; 119:47 11 t. Psalm 119; compare Isa 56:6 ; compare also of love to Jerusalem 66:10 ; Psa 122:6 . 4 especially Participle אֹהֵב = ( a ) lover , Lam 1:2 (figurative of Jerusalem); ( b ) friend Hiram of David 1Kin 5:15 , compare Jer 20:4 , 6 ; Est 5:10 , 14 ; 6:13 ; Psa 38:12 (|| רֵעַ ) so Psalm 88:19, Prov 14:20 ; also 18:24 ; 27:6 ; Abraham of God Isa 41:8 ; 2Chr 20:7 . 5 of divine love ( a ) to individual men Deut 4:37 ; 2Sam 12:24 ; Prov 3:12 ; 15:9 ; Psa 146:8 ; Neh 13:26 ; ( b ) to people Israel, etc. Deut 7:8 , 13 ; 23:6 ; Hosea 3:1 ; 9:15 ; 11:1 ; 14:5 ; 1Kin 10:9 ; 2Chr 2:10 ; 9:8 ; Isa 43:4 ; 48:14 ; Jer 31:3 ; Mal 1:2 (3 t. in verse); Psa 47:5 ; to Jerusalem 78:68 ; 87:2 ; ( c ) to righteousness, etc. 11:7 ; 33:5 ; 37:28 ; 45:8 ; 99:4 ; Isa 61:8 ; Mal 2:11 . Niph`al Participle plural הַנֶּאֱהָבִים 2Sam 1:23 lovely, loveable of Saul & Jonath. (|| הַנְּעִימִם ). Pi`el Participle plural suffix מְאַהֲבַי (בָֿ֑י) Hosea 2:7 3 t.; מְאַהֲבַיִח (בָֿ֑יִח) Jer 22:20 6 t.; מְאַהֲבֶיהָ Hosea 2:9 4 t. 1 friends Zech 13:6 ; 2 lovers in figure of adulterous Israel Hosea 2:7 ; 2:9 ; 2:12 ; 2:14 ; 2:15 ; Ezek 23:5 , 9 ; Judah Jer 22:20 , 22 ; 30:14 ; Lam 1:19 ; Ezek 16:33 , 36 , 37 ; 23:22 .","rootNote":"or אָהֵב ; a